This file only exists so git tracks the (otherwise empty) data/ directory.

The actual database file (demonicslots.sqlite, plus its WAL sidecar files)
is created here at runtime and is gitignored - see ../.gitignore.

This directory existing on disk *before* the systemd service starts
matters: deploy/demonicslots-backend.service uses ProtectSystem=strict
with ReadWritePaths pointing at this directory, and systemd needs that
path to already exist to bind-mount it as the one writable exception in
an otherwise read-only filesystem view. If it doesn't exist yet, the
service fails to start with "Result: resources" (see backend/README.md's
troubleshooting note).
